{
    "background_story": "Kaiden was a brilliant materials scientist who had always been fascinated by the concept of porosity. Growing up, he spent hours watching water seep through the soil in his backyard, mesmerized by the way it flowed through the tiny pores. As he delved deeper into his research, Kaiden became obsessed with creating materials that could mimic the natural world's ability to absorb and filter. His breakthrough came when he developed a revolutionary new membrane with unprecedented porosity. The membrane was capable of filtering even the smallest impurities from water, making it safe for drinking in some of the world's most polluted regions. Kaiden's discovery earned him international recognition and accolades, but more importantly, it brought clean water to countless communities in need.",
